# act configuration (https://github.com/nektos/act): run `act` with the same
# options every time, from the repository root.
#
# -W: only the CI workflow.
#
# -P: act cannot run the macOS or Windows runners - everything runs in Linux
#     containers - so every label of the matrix maps to the same image. The
#     ghcr.io mirror is used because Docker Hub limits anonymous pulls on this
#     network (HTTP 429 Too Many Requests), and the mirror carries the same
#     catthehacker image.
#
# --concurrent-jobs: three jobs at a time keeps Docker Desktop responsive
#     while the 3x3 test matrix runs.
#
# --rm: remove the containers even when a job fails; the log already keeps
#     the output of every step.
-W .github/workflows/ci.yml
-P ubuntu-latest=ghcr.io/catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest
-P macos-latest=ghcr.io/catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest
-P windows-latest=ghcr.io/catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest
--concurrent-jobs 3
--rm
